>>> not a link 
mhttp://www.foo.com
<<<
<p>mhttp://www.foo.com</p>
>>> following a newline
m
http://www.foo.com
<<<
<p>m
<a href="http://www.foo.com">http://www.foo.com</a></p>
>>> invalid domain run with underscores and repeated www.
www._www._a
<<<
<p>www._www._a</p>
>>> unmatched interior closing parentheses before trailing parenthesis
www.example.com/a)b) and www.example.com/a))b(c)
<<<
<p><a href="http://www.example.com/a)b">www.example.com/a)b</a>) and <a href="http://www.example.com/a))b(c">www.example.com/a))b(c</a>)</p>
>>> url schemes, www boundary, and email with special characters
https://example.com and ftp://example.com and awww.example.com and foo+bar-baz.qux@example.com
<<<
<p><a href="https://example.com">https://example.com</a> and <a href="ftp://example.com">ftp://example.com</a> and awww.example.com and <a href="mailto:foo+bar-baz.qux@example.com">foo+bar-baz.qux@example.com</a></p>
>>> email autolink where a URL autolink cannot start
/www.a.b@c.d and /foo@bar.com and xhttp://a.b
<<<
<p>/<a href="mailto:www.a.b@c.d">www.a.b@c.d</a> and /<a href="mailto:foo@bar.com">foo@bar.com</a> and xhttp://a.b</p>
>>> percent-encoded characters are not double-encoded
https://example.com/%40foo?q=%26 and www.example.com/%e2%82%AC
<<<
<p><a href="https://example.com/%40foo?q=%26">https://example.com/%40foo?q=%26</a> and <a href="http://www.example.com/%e2%82%AC">www.example.com/%e2%82%AC</a></p>
>>> invalid percent-encoding and other characters are still encoded
https://example.com/%zz%4/%%41/fü
<<<
<p><a href="https://example.com/%25zz%254/%25%41/f%C3%BC">https://example.com/%zz%4/%%41/fü</a></p>
